@startuml cp1-sequence
title Kafka Experiment: Producer and Consumer — Observed Interaction

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

actor Developer as dev

participant "ingestion-poller\n(Producer)" as Producer #DBEAFE
participant "Redpanda\nadsb.raw — Partition 0" as Broker #FEF9C3
participant "position-consumer\n(Consumer)" as Consumer #DBEAFE
participant "__consumer_offsets\n(Redpanda internal)" as Offsets #F3E8FF

== Consumer startup ==

dev -> Consumer : tsx src/consume.ts
Consumer -> Broker : connect()\n+ version handshake
Consumer -> Broker : subscribe(adsb.raw, fromBeginning: true)

note right of Broker
  No committed offset exists for kafka-experiment yet.
  fromBeginning: true — start from LOG-START-OFFSET = 1.
  (Offset 0 was deleted by retention between sessions.)
end note

Broker --> Consumer : deliver offset 1\n{"checkpoint":5, "source":"manual-store-verification"}
Consumer -> Consumer : eachMessage handler

Broker --> Consumer : deliver offset 2\n{"checkpoint":5, "source":"manual-store-verification"}
Consumer -> Consumer : eachMessage handler

note right of Consumer
  Consumer is now idle. Current position (in memory) = 3.
  No committed offset yet — autoCommit has not fired.
  Waiting for new records.
end note

== Producer run (second terminal) ==

dev -> Producer : tsx src/produce.ts
Producer -> Broker : connect()
Producer -> Broker : ProduceRequest\nkey: "test-aircraft-1"\nvalue: {entity_id, timestamp_ms: 1787173715941}

Broker -> Broker : append to partition log\nassign offset 3\nHIGH-WATERMARK: 3 → 4

Broker --> Producer : RecordMetadata\n(partition=0, baseOffset="3")
Producer -> Broker : disconnect()

== Delivery ==

Broker --> Consumer : deliver offset 3\n{entity_id: "test-aircraft-1", timestamp_ms: 1787173715941}

note right of Consumer
  Same millisecond timestamp as the ProduceRequest.
  Partition 0, offset 3, key and payload match exactly.
end note

Consumer -> Consumer : eachMessage handler

== autoCommit (background timer, fires ~5s after handler returns) ==

Consumer -> Broker : commit offset\nkafka-experiment :: adsb.raw[0] = 4
Broker -> Offsets : persist\nkafka-experiment: CURRENT-OFFSET = 4

note over Consumer, Offsets
  CURRENT-OFFSET = 4 means "next fetch starts at offset 4".
  Offset 3 is now the committed resume point.
  On clean restart: resumes from 4, offset 3 not re-delivered.
  On crash before this commit fires: offset 3 re-delivered on restart.
end note

== Crash recovery experiment (simulated with rpk group seek) ==

dev -> Broker : rpk group seek kafka-experiment --to start

Broker -> Offsets : reset kafka-experiment\nCURRENT-OFFSET: 4 → 1

note right of Offsets
  Simulates a crash before autoCommit fired.
  LAG is now 3 (offsets 1, 2, 3 unconsumed by this group again).
end note

dev -> Consumer : tsx src/consume.ts (restart)
Consumer -> Broker : connect() + rejoin group
Consumer -> Broker : fetch from CURRENT-OFFSET = 1

Broker --> Consumer : re-deliver offset 1
Broker --> Consumer : re-deliver offset 2
Broker --> Consumer : re-deliver offset 3\n{entity_id: "test-aircraft-1"} — same payload, second time

note right of Consumer
  At-least-once delivery.
  The same event was processed twice with identical payload.
  This is why TimescaleDB uses ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  and Redis checks timestamps before overwriting.
end note

@enduml
